---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const CALENDLY = "https://calendly.com/alanyowu/30min";
---
<Layout
  title="Margin: AI copilot for dealer-group CFOs"
  description="Margin answers every dealer-finance question with a verbatim quote and page citation from an OEM accounting manual or NADA benchmark, or refuses on the record. Built by Alan Wu, a Cornell engineer currently interviewing dealer finance people."
  current=""
>
  <section class="pt-10 md:pt-16 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-6">
      cite or refuse
    </p>

    <h1 class="font-serif hero">
      <span class="text-[var(--color-life)]">Margin</span> is an AI copilot for dealer-group CFOs.
    </h1>

    <p class="mt-8 max-w-2xl font-serif text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink)]/80">
      Every answer is a verbatim quote with a page citation from an OEM accounting
      manual or NADA benchmark, or a refusal on the record when the source
      doesn't say so. The hard rule <em>is</em> the product.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-24 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-6">
      why this exists
    </h2>
    <p class="summary">
      The factory statement tells a dealer an expense is 5% of gross. What it
      won't tell you is <em>which</em> gross. The number can pull from a
      different page than the one you're reading, so controllers and CFOs back
      into it by hand, every month. Margin reads the OEM Dealer Standard
      Accounting Manuals, the NADA benchmarks, and the regulatory references,
      then answers with the exact page that defines the number, side by side
      with the source.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 max-w-2xl">
    <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-[var(--color-mute)] mb-6">
      who's building it
    </h2>
    <p class="summary">
      I'm <span class="grow-line wake font-medium">Alan Wu</span>, a Cornell
      engineer building Margin. It's early. No polished product yet, and this
      isn't a sales pitch. I'm talking to controllers, dealer-group CFOs, and
      the CPA firms who serve them so I build something that earns its place in
      your month-end. If you live in the factory statement, I'd value 20 minutes
      on how you close and reconcile it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-20 mb-24 max-w-2xl">
    <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-rule)] pt-8">
      <p class="font-serif text-lg text-[var(--color-ink)]/90 mb-6">
        20 minutes, no pitch. Just tell me where the statement lies to you.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 font-mono text-sm">
        <a href={CALENDLY} class="grow-line wake">&rarr; book a time</a>
        <a href="/" class="grow-line wake text-[var(--color-mute)]">&rarr; more about me</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
